<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds drifted along with the foreign trend in thin volumes and traders saw little to shake the market out of its end-year stupor.</p>
<p>&quot;The market is gaining in line with the foreign sentiment but nobody is interested in doing too much,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>&quot;The lack of liquidity will be evident throughout the session and I don't see it changing until the New Year,&quot; added another.</p>
<p>Turnover on the benchmark 10-year cash market was a mere 8,420. --Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
